From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Sep 27 23:57:20 2000
From: Scott Brewster <scott () ses-sb ! its ! dias ! qut ! edu ! au>
Date: Wed, 27 Sep 2000 23:57:20 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: [SUMMARY] libcurses.so in OSFOBSOLETE subset
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=97009896821183

Hi,

Problem: Is the libcurses.so library with version `osf.1' available
for Compaq Tru64 UNIX V5.0A?

Solution: It was part of the OSFOBSOLETE subset in the 4.0 stream, but has
not shipped with the 5.0 stream. Solutions are to upgrade the application
so that it uses the `xpg4' version of the library, or to copy the obsolete
library from a 4.0 box, which seems to work, but is, of course, unsupported.

Thanks to Dr. Tom Blinn and Pat Lampert.

The original message appears below.

Scott

> Hi,
> 
> One of our users has an old application that requires the library
> `libcurses.so' with version `osf.1'. The version of the library
> that is currently on our Tru64 UNIX V5.0A machine is `xpg4'.
> 
> In the `OSFOBSOLETE425' subset there was a copy of the older
> `osf.1' version of the library, but this does not appear to
> be in the `OSFOBSOLETE505' subset that comes with the 5.0A operating
> system.
> 
> Is the library available for Tru64 UNIX V5.0A? Can we simply copy the
> old library from a Digital UNIX 4.0D machine and set `LD_LIBRARY_PATH'
> appropriately?
> 
> Attached is a message from the `Progress Knowledgebase'.
> 
> Scott
> 
>    --- Start Extract ---
>    Kbase Id:
>    17866
>    Title:
>    Digital UNIX 4.00D libcurses.so library
>    Digital UNIX 4.00D libcurses.so library
>    DRAFT COPY  -  Currently under review and edit.
>    INTRODUCTION:
>    =============
>    When upgrading Digital UNIX version 4.00B to 4.00D Progress cannot run
>    anymore because of a library version mismatch.
>    WHY YOU NEED TO KNOW THIS:
>    ===========================
>    Pre 4.00D versions of Digital UNIX used the libcurses.so library with
>    version OSF.1. Version 4.00D has the new XPG4 version of the libcurses
>    library. Progress cannot use this library with version 8.2 so will
>    abort with an error describing this.
>    PROCEDURAL APPROACH:
>    ====================
>    The fix is to install the "Nonconforming Curses Library", which is in
>    the OSFOBSOLETE425 subset on the Digital UNIX 4.00D OS Disk.
>    This is documented on page 8-2 of the Digital UNIX: Release notes for
>    version 4.0D manual, in chapter 8 "Features and Interfaces Scheduled
>    for Retirement".
>    ONLINE PROCEDURES OR UTILITIES:
>    ===============================
>    REFERENCES TO WRITTEN DOCUMENTATION:   
>    ====================================   
>    Progress Software Technical Support Note # 17866
>    --- End Extract ---

