from  <mailto:alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com> alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com 
 
The mount(8) command will provide a list of file systems
mounted on a particular system. If any fileset on a
domain is mounted, then it is probably unwise to have
a fileset of that domain mounted elsewhere. Each file-
set corresponds to a mounted file system that you'd
see with the mount command. I think this will give
you enough information to work something out.
Since your method of report generation relies on a 2nd
copy that suggests you have the space for a 2nd copy
of any particular domain or fileset. You might want
to see if the firmware version of the controller in the
SW800 supports the CLONE command (a "RUN" command). It
may be possible to clone the data this way.
