X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96955304414663

Great list, as always!

Thanks go to
  Dr. Tom Blinn
  Colin Walters
  Nikola Milutinovic

I missed one subset from the OS cd. As Dr. Tom Blinn pointed:

---------
It should be on the base OS cd media, as one of the optional subsets.

Put your base OS cdrom disk 1 into the CDROM reader, mount it on some
handy mount point (lets assume it's mounted on /cdrom), and then use
the setld utility to see that optional subsets are not loaded on your
system:

# mount -r /dev/rz<unit>c /cdrom
# setld -l /cdrom

Or use "setld -i" to get a list of all the subsets that were available
to your system at installation time:

# setld -i

and look for "Single-Byte European Locales (System Administration)" or
something like that.  It's probably not installed on your system.  If
it is installed, you just need to configure it.
---------

Original question bellow.

Regards,

Manuel Monteiro


