of the machines. The card failed and I replaced it with the same model 
card in the same slot.  Originally the devices were named tu0 - tu3.  
After replacing the card the devices for the card were now tu4 - tu7.

I would like to again have the devices named tu0 - tu4.

How can I do this?

The man page for hwmgr implies that I can use hwmgr to delete devices 
and then they can be renumbered:


  -delete name
      Deletes a hardware persistence entry. When you delete a hardware com-
      ponent it cannot be used. For example, if the system has a network
      adapter named tu0 and you add a second network adapter in a lower slot,
      the new adapter will be automatically named tu1.  However, if you
      delete tu0 then both adapters will be automatically renamed in the
      order they are discovered (when the system probes buses and controll-
      ers).  The new network adapter in the lower slot becomes tu0 and the
      original adapter is renamed to tu1. (See also the -remove operation.)

I can delete the tu0 - tu3, but cannot delete tu4 which is the running 
port and in any event the man page does not explain how to initiate a 
bus probe.



