 A few sent email with tips on how to get the "steam" agent to talk to the
subsystem. But I reminded them that the agent was talking to the subsystem
as the "CLI" client could connect. It appeared to be a client problem on the
NT side, and it was.

 The solution to our problem with v2.3 of the StorageWorks Command Console
(SWCC) not detecting the subsystem when using the HSG80ACS8.5 client was;

 To remove the previous install with "Start->Settings->Control
Panel->Add/Remove Programs" (remove ALL the SWCC products). And then remove
all references in the registry and then remove the remaining installation
directories off of the disk. The manual removal of the registry entries and
the old install directories was the difference. We had previously followed
the installation instructions and just removed the old v2.1 software. But a
simple remove was not good enough, apparently.

 Basically, it needs to be a "first time" install. Typical of NT
applications, they do not remove without a trace and reinstalls many times
do not work.

 It is hard for us Unix types to like NT ;-)

Thanks to everyone who helped out.

Dan Goetzman

