Hello Admins,


Need some help on an Alpha 200 workstation.  It had 4.d on it and I am
trying to upgrade to 4.0f.  I have 7 of them.  I upgraded the firmware
on the first one and all hell broke loose.  It tried to come up with
Windows NT of all things.  I kept messing around reloading the firmware
and finally got it to take.  Upgraded to 4.0f just fine.  Went to the
second one and the same thing happened.  All I did was boot the firmware
cd and update the SRM and ARC.  Recycled the power and it tries to boot
Windows NT again.  It shows the default boot type as Digital Unix but
for some reason keeps reverting back to NT.  I did notice that the SRM
updated to version 7.0 but the ARC says 4.8.  Any suggestions on what
might be causing this??

darryl

