Greetings...

Thanks to Octave Orgeron who hit this one right on the head. 

> I have seen this problem before in Digital's
> implementation of CDE. You are more than likely
> running in 24-bit colour mode. You'll have to switch
> back to 8-bit mode for the Style Manager to work
> properly and then switch back to 24-bit colour when
> you are done customizing.

I modified /var/X11/Xserver.conf from:
 -vclass TrueColor
to
 -vclass PseudoColor
 
The style manager is once again capable of creating custom palettes however only 
256 colors won't cut it. So as Octave recommends, create the custom palette and 
then modify Xserver.conf back to it original setting.

Thanks also to Colin Walters. Don't forget about:
/etc/dt/config/<lang>/sys.resources

/mark

